1
00:00:15,029 --> 00:00:18,868
<i>SAWYER FARM
ESTABLISHED 1845

2
00:00:20,494 --> 00:00:29,548
<i># Happy birthday to you...

3
00:00:29,672 --> 00:00:34,513
<i># Happy birthday, dear Jed...

4
00:00:34,720 --> 00:00:39,434
<i># Happy birthday to you...

5
00:00:39,559 --> 00:00:41,271
All right, now make a wish.

6
00:00:41,306 --> 00:00:42,273
Blow them out.

7
00:00:47,068 --> 00:00:49,321
Yes! Very good!

8
00:00:49,362 --> 00:00:51,532
Yes, yes, yes, yes!

9
00:00:51,573 --> 00:00:52,784
Very good!

10
00:00:52,908 --> 00:00:54,202
All right...

11
00:00:58,040 --> 00:01:00,086
Drayton, where are your manners?

12
00:01:00,169 --> 00:01:02,338
Give the first slice to the thief.

13
00:01:17,105 --> 00:01:18,586
I didn't steal your damn pigs...

14
00:01:18,621 --> 00:01:20,068
Are you calling my son a liar?

15
00:01:20,193 --> 00:01:22,446
He saw your filthy hands stealing our property...

16
00:01:27,032 --> 00:01:29,829
Why would I go anywhere near your filthy pigs?

17
00:01:29,953 --> 00:01:31,415
Or your filthy family!

18
00:01:31,498 --> 00:01:34,585
I swear, everybody will know what kind of...

19
00:01:34,626 --> 00:01:36,504
...offspring you're raising here, Verna!

20
00:01:36,586 --> 00:01:38,423
Shut him up! I've had enough!

21
00:01:40,300 --> 00:01:41,933
Listen to me, no farmhand is going to...

22
00:01:41,968 --> 00:01:43,764
...ruin my son's special night.

23
00:01:47,017 --> 00:01:48,394
Ready for your present?

24
00:01:51,689 --> 00:01:53,692
You know you're my special boy.

25
00:01:54,275 --> 00:01:56,362
Come on, Jed. There you go...

26
00:01:59,199 --> 00:02:01,452
- Jed.
- Yes, that's it, Jed.

27
00:02:03,955 --> 00:02:04,999
Now remember,

28
00:02:05,207 --> 00:02:08,336
bad people like him try to destroy our family.

29
00:02:08,961 --> 00:02:10,756
But we won't let that happen, will we?

30
00:02:10,922 --> 00:02:12,298
Go on, pick it up...

31
00:02:13,091 --> 00:02:14,593
Jed, pick it up...

32
00:02:15,134 --> 00:02:15,970
Jed!

33
00:02:16,094 --> 00:02:19,723
Jed...

34
00:02:19,764 --> 00:02:21,310
Pick it up, Jed!

35
00:02:21,351 --> 00:02:24,647
Jed!

36
00:02:25,480 --> 00:02:27,441
Come on, you know what you have to do...

37
00:02:27,858 --> 00:02:29,571
That's it, Jed!

38
00:02:31,780 --> 00:02:32,991
Come on, Jed...

39
00:02:33,699 --> 00:02:36,537
Jed!

40
00:02:36,619 --> 00:02:38,080
No!

41
00:02:38,121 --> 00:02:39,374
There you go.

42
00:02:39,790 --> 00:02:41,042
Go on, son!

43
00:02:41,077 --> 00:02:42,378
No!

44
00:02:49,092 --> 00:02:50,804
No!

45
00:02:56,394 --> 00:02:58,481
No!

46
00:02:58,647 --> 00:03:00,483
No, please!

47
00:03:00,608 --> 00:03:03,403
No!

48
00:03:03,444 --> 00:03:06,073
Do it, do it, do it!

49
00:03:06,114 --> 00:03:08,075
No!

50
00:03:08,116 --> 00:03:09,827
Go on, Jed, do it...

51
00:03:10,786 --> 00:03:11,830
Do it!

52
00:03:12,414 --> 00:03:14,626
- Jed.
- Do it!

53
00:03:20,923 --> 00:03:22,051
Mom!

54
00:03:22,800 --> 00:03:24,094
Mom, no!

55
00:03:25,846 --> 00:03:29,185
No!

56
00:03:39,071 --> 00:03:39,906
Hey.

57
00:03:40,197 --> 00:03:41,784
You let us down, Jed.

58
00:03:44,536 --> 00:03:47,623
It's all right. Family will always be here for
you.

59
00:03:47,789 --> 00:03:49,124
Remember that.

60
00:03:49,875 --> 00:03:50,918
All right.

61
00:04:08,606 --> 00:04:13,697
<i>TEXAS, 1955

62
00:04:16,698 --> 00:04:18,119
Are you trying to get us killed?

63
00:04:18,159 --> 00:04:19,036
Do you want me to stop?

64
00:04:19,078 --> 00:04:20,329
No, I didn't say that.

65
00:04:27,630 --> 00:04:28,716
Watch out!

66
00:04:33,429 --> 00:04:35,225
What the hell was that thing?

67
00:04:36,516 --> 00:04:37,728
Hey, Betty.

68
00:04:44,943 --> 00:04:46,195
What is it?

69
00:04:47,487 --> 00:04:48,615
I don't know.

70
00:04:51,868 --> 00:04:53,330
Then let's go.

71
00:05:02,380 --> 00:05:03,592
What?

72
00:05:11,976 --> 00:05:13,312
He's just a kid!

73
00:05:15,356 --> 00:05:16,650
Let's go!

74
00:05:17,024 --> 00:05:18,443
We'll be late.

75
00:05:20,570 --> 00:05:22,072
Hello.

76
00:05:26,328 --> 00:05:27,622
Are you okay?

77
00:05:33,753 --> 00:05:35,798
You shouldn't play in the road.

78
00:05:35,964 --> 00:05:37,925
Help me, please...

79
00:05:44,100 --> 00:05:46,061
Hey, Betty, where are you going? I didn't hit him!

80
00:05:46,477 --> 00:05:48,105
- Something's wrong.
- Betty!

81
00:05:48,145 --> 00:05:49,565
He needs help.

82
00:05:50,107 --> 00:05:51,525
Jesus Christ!

83
00:05:55,947 --> 00:05:57,909
Hey, buddy, can you hear me?

84
00:05:59,911 --> 00:06:01,454
Let me help you!

85
00:06:05,332 --> 00:06:06,501
Hello?

86
00:06:13,133 --> 00:06:15,722
It's okay. You can come out.

87
00:06:17,179 --> 00:06:18,308
Betty.

88
00:06:22,103 --> 00:06:23,814
Betty, where did you go?

89
00:07:22,094 --> 00:07:23,389
Hello?

90
00:07:28,561 --> 00:07:32,107
Come on... I won't hurt you.

91
00:07:34,650 --> 00:07:36,153
I just want to help...

92
00:07:43,203 --> 00:07:44,372
Okay?

93
00:07:55,261 --> 00:07:59,558
<i>BASED ON CHARACTERS CREATED BY

94
00:07:59,640 --> 00:08:02,604
<i>KIM HENKEL AND TOBE HOOPER

95
00:08:04,897 --> 00:08:06,941
You did good, Jed!

96
00:08:07,733 --> 00:08:10,779
It's like... I can still feel you in there
after all.

97
00:08:42,107 --> 00:08:45,696
Well, let him learn a little more.

98
00:08:49,157 --> 00:08:50,702
Oh, my God!

99
00:09:00,338 --> 00:09:01,257
Show him!

100
00:09:14,480 --> 00:09:15,857
- Where is she?
- Calm down, Hal.

101
00:09:16,357 --> 00:09:17,944
Let me through, damn it!

102
00:09:17,985 --> 00:09:19,530
Let me go! Let me go, damn it!

103
00:09:19,570 --> 00:09:21,155
- We know what happened.
- Calm down, Hal.

104
00:09:21,321 --> 00:09:22,950
Is that my little girl in there?

105
00:09:24,451 --> 00:09:27,330
Is she in there? Is my little girl in there?

106
00:09:27,664 --> 00:09:29,041
Answer me, damn it!

107
00:09:29,374 --> 00:09:30,751
We've got one of them.

108
00:09:35,130 --> 00:09:36,509
Oh, boy!

109
00:09:40,679 --> 00:09:42,057
I couldn't get to her in time!

110
00:09:42,265 --> 00:09:44,310
I'm so sorry, sir. I swear to God.

111
00:09:46,811 --> 00:09:48,522
Drayton Sawyer...

112
00:09:51,024 --> 00:09:52,903
It's time to go to Gorman Reformatory.

113
00:09:52,944 --> 00:09:56,283
No... You're all grown up now.

114
00:09:58,534 --> 00:10:00,538
That means the gas chamber for you.

115
00:10:04,208 --> 00:10:05,462
Why?

116
00:10:05,794 --> 00:10:07,631
Are you going to arrest me for finding a dead
body?

117
00:10:07,838 --> 00:10:09,300
Last I checked, that wasn't a crime.

118
00:10:09,349 --> 00:10:12,103
How about a bullet hole in your damn skull?

119
00:10:12,769 --> 00:10:14,069
- Put it away, Hal.
- Come on.

120
00:10:14,104 --> 00:10:15,982
He's right. We've got nothing on him...

121
00:10:16,356 --> 00:10:17,565
Calm down, Hal.

122
00:10:17,773 --> 00:10:18,525
Keep your head clear.

123
00:10:18,565 --> 00:10:21,069
- Hal, it's not worth it.
- Come on, Hal, lower the gun.

124
00:10:21,193 --> 00:10:22,529
Damn trash.

125
00:10:33,705 --> 00:10:35,666
Let those boys go right this instant!

126
00:10:35,957 --> 00:10:37,626
Don't count on it, Verna!

127
00:10:38,376 --> 00:10:39,837
Do you think they did anything wrong?

128
00:10:39,877 --> 00:10:40,963
No, I don't!

129
00:10:41,045 --> 00:10:42,881
You bastard, let them out of the car!

130
00:10:43,381 --> 00:10:46,176
No! They're going to stay there and rot!

131
00:10:47,259 --> 00:10:48,344
On what charges?

132
00:10:48,635 --> 00:10:49,929
They're not under arrest.

133
00:10:49,970 --> 00:10:52,265
They're in protective custody... from you.

134
00:10:52,306 --> 00:10:53,558
What are you talking about?

135
00:10:54,558 --> 00:10:57,103
I can't count how many crime scenes I've been
to...

136
00:10:57,144 --> 00:10:59,481
...where there's always a Sawyer involved.

137
00:11:00,023 --> 00:11:01,816
Those boys aren't safe with you...

138
00:11:01,898 --> 00:11:03,026
Bullshit.

139
00:11:03,942 --> 00:11:06,280
Get a warrant for the Sawyer house.

140
00:11:06,612 --> 00:11:08,657
Name every one of them. I want them all.

141
00:11:08,823 --> 00:11:09,825
- Did you hear me?
- You can't do that.

142
00:11:09,907 --> 00:11:10,784
You can't do that!

143
00:11:10,867 --> 00:11:12,578
Well, by the time we get there, I'll have a
warrant saying I can...

144
00:11:12,660 --> 00:11:14,121
...do just that.

145
00:11:14,787 --> 00:11:16,914
It's called "children at risk."

146
00:11:18,332 --> 00:11:20,293
You took one of mine...

147
00:11:21,043 --> 00:11:23,463
...so I'll take every one of yours, Verna.

148
00:11:29,635 --> 00:11:31,011
Every last one of them...

149
00:11:33,013 --> 00:11:35,016
<i>10 YEARS LATER

150
00:11:35,474 --> 00:11:39,145
<i>In 1935, the state of Texas established a...

151
00:11:39,186 --> 00:11:41,689
<i>...program to care for children at risk.

152
00:11:41,855 --> 00:11:45,193
In its first year, nearly 52 children were
removed from homes...

153
00:11:45,274 --> 00:11:48,111
...known to be involved in criminal activity.

154
00:11:48,444 --> 00:11:51,324
<i>Many of these children were given new names...

155
00:11:51,365 --> 00:11:53,159
<i>...and placed in foster homes.

156
00:11:53,283 --> 00:11:56,871
<i>Others, products of degenerate parenting...

157
00:11:56,912 --> 00:11:59,749
<i>...ended up here at Gorman Reformatory.

158
00:11:59,790 --> 00:12:01,165
<i>GORMAN HOUSE JUVENILE REFORMATORY

159
00:12:01,206 --> 00:12:05,336
We take care of their physical and
psychological needs.

160
00:12:05,794 --> 00:12:07,047
Yes, sir.

161
00:12:07,171 --> 00:12:09,967
I've wanted to come here for a long time.

162
00:12:10,257 --> 00:12:11,593
I think I can help them.

163
00:12:11,759 --> 00:12:12,803
Elizabeth.

164
00:12:12,843 --> 00:12:14,471
Please, sir, Lizzy. Lizzy is fine.

165
00:12:14,512 --> 00:12:16,013
Elizabeth.

166
00:12:16,972 --> 00:12:19,225
Most of these children will end up...

167
00:12:19,265 --> 00:12:21,477
...in prisons or mental institutions.

168
00:12:22,519 --> 00:12:25,983
Keeping them here makes everyone safer.

169
00:12:26,774 --> 00:12:28,026
Keep your guard up.

170
00:13:12,694 --> 00:13:14,071
Well... hello...

171
00:13:14,904 --> 00:13:16,365
My name is Lizzy.

172
00:13:16,448 --> 00:13:19,327
I'm new here, and I'd like to get to know you.

173
00:13:23,872 --> 00:13:25,207
That's Bud.

174
00:13:26,833 --> 00:13:29,209
He doesn't say much for such a big guy.

175
00:13:34,632 --> 00:13:35,634
You're in my seat.

176
00:13:36,175 --> 00:13:37,344
I'm sorry.

177
00:13:38,218 --> 00:13:40,221
- Very nice.
- I'm...

178
00:13:40,262 --> 00:13:42,307
Lizzy... Yeah, I heard. I heard.

179
00:13:43,306 --> 00:13:45,476
Shit, sorry. I'm Jackson.

180
00:13:46,267 --> 00:13:49,230
Jackson and... Bud...

181
00:13:50,022 --> 00:13:52,484
And what medication are you taking, Jackson?

182
00:13:52,650 --> 00:13:53,860
Medication?

183
00:13:55,069 --> 00:13:57,030
They already gave it to us when they brought
us in, right?

184
00:13:58,029 --> 00:14:00,949
We figured you'd know more about that than we
do, Lizzy...

185
00:14:01,949 --> 00:14:04,371
You're not going to give me any trouble, are you?

186
00:14:04,870 --> 00:14:06,331
No, not me, Lizzy.

187
00:14:07,665 --> 00:14:08,964
Is there a reason you keep...

188
00:14:08,999 --> 00:14:10,543
...saying my name like that?

189
00:14:11,126 --> 00:14:15,380
No... I just like to know who's in charge,
that's all.

190
00:14:18,465 --> 00:14:20,135
Fuck you, asshole!

191
00:14:20,176 --> 00:14:21,095
I'll kick your ass.

192
00:14:21,135 --> 00:14:22,888
I'll fuck up your head!

193
00:14:23,012 --> 00:14:24,098
Let him go!

194
00:14:24,138 --> 00:14:25,683
Mind your own business!

195
00:14:25,807 --> 00:14:27,190
It is my business.

196
00:14:27,225 --> 00:14:28,643
What's the problem?

197
00:14:29,142 --> 00:14:31,562
He said something I didn't like.

198
00:14:31,853 --> 00:14:35,358
About what a girl in a nurse's uniform would
taste like.

199
00:14:36,233 --> 00:14:37,820
Hey, hey, let go of me!

200
00:14:38,111 --> 00:14:39,488
Let go!

201
00:14:40,321 --> 00:14:41,907
Fuck you, Frankenstein!

202
00:14:41,948 --> 00:14:43,574
That's enough. Stop it.

203
00:14:43,949 --> 00:14:46,370
- Ike, what did you do?
- I didn't do anything.

204
00:14:49,414 --> 00:14:50,624
Everything's fine.

205
00:15:51,599 --> 00:15:53,226
What are you doing?

206
00:15:58,188 --> 00:15:59,482
Come here.

207
00:16:02,818 --> 00:16:04,321
What's the problem?

208
00:16:04,362 --> 00:16:06,198
It's just a stupid mouse.

209
00:16:09,075 --> 00:16:10,369
Got a light?

210
00:16:10,451 --> 00:16:12,286
You know smoking isn't allowed in here...

211
00:16:14,579 --> 00:16:16,958
I have special permission.

212
00:16:17,750 --> 00:16:19,002
True story.

213
00:16:19,043 --> 00:16:20,963
Ask Dr. Lang.

214
00:16:21,170 --> 00:16:22,005
I will.

215
00:16:22,046 --> 00:16:24,007
He'll tell you it helps me.

216
00:16:25,091 --> 00:16:27,717
With my anxiety.

217
00:16:30,970 --> 00:16:32,514
The truth is...

218
00:16:33,555 --> 00:16:35,685
...it's because I'm his favorite.

219
00:16:36,059 --> 00:16:37,521
He told me so.

220
00:16:37,728 --> 00:16:40,398
- You've earned yourself a warning.
- Why?

221
00:16:40,438 --> 00:16:41,983
I was just taking a bath.

222
00:16:42,023 --> 00:16:43,359
Get out.

223
00:16:46,778 --> 00:16:48,072
Bitch.

224
00:16:49,906 --> 00:16:51,660
Is everything all right?

225
00:16:52,368 --> 00:16:54,579
Yes, Doctor, I'm fine.

226
00:16:55,161 --> 00:17:00,042
I'll handle Isaac and Bud.

227
00:17:00,125 --> 00:17:01,877
No. Bud didn't do anything.

228
00:17:01,918 --> 00:17:04,317
I look forward to our session tomorrow, Jackson.

229
00:17:04,352 --> 00:17:06,716
I'm sorry, but he's actually right.

230
00:17:06,756 --> 00:17:08,051
Bud didn't do anything.

231
00:17:08,092 --> 00:17:10,218
He was fighting...

232
00:17:10,843 --> 00:17:12,512
Well, he was protecting me...

233
00:17:12,594 --> 00:17:13,847
Remind me to tell you later what...

234
00:17:13,887 --> 00:17:15,473
...he did to his last foster family.

235
00:17:15,556 --> 00:17:17,225
Well, they took his dog away.

236
00:17:17,766 --> 00:17:21,062
Yes... that's a perfectly good reason...

237
00:17:21,103 --> 00:17:23,732
...to put someone in a coma.

238
00:17:24,107 --> 00:17:25,608
Well, I'm just saying.

239
00:17:48,046 --> 00:17:48,964
<i>DIAGNOSIS: BIPOLAR DISORDER

240
00:17:49,005 --> 00:17:52,926
<i>Upon admission, this 16-year-old boy,
Horton, Bud, was depressed, agitated and
fearful.

241
00:17:53,051 --> 00:17:56,094
<i>Overall, his behavior was aggressive,
unusually energetic and withdrawn.

242
00:17:59,306 --> 00:18:01,142
Sorry, I didn't mean to scare you.

243
00:18:01,892 --> 00:18:03,227
You didn't.

244
00:18:03,977 --> 00:18:05,563
Thank you for helping Bud.

245
00:18:06,647 --> 00:18:10,275
I know you don't even know him, so that was nice.

246
00:18:11,025 --> 00:18:13,945
Well, I'm here to help you all. So...

247
00:18:15,697 --> 00:18:17,992
You're the first pretty nurse we've had around
here.

248
00:18:20,869 --> 00:18:22,455
So I thought you should know...

249
00:18:23,956 --> 00:18:25,124
Know what?

250
00:18:25,457 --> 00:18:28,087
What goes on in the relaxation room...

251
00:18:29,003 --> 00:18:30,882
The kids around here call it...

252
00:18:31,048 --> 00:18:33,301
...Dr. Lang's chamber of horrors.

253
00:18:33,717 --> 00:18:35,303
Piece of shit.

254
00:18:36,220 --> 00:18:37,138
Why is that?

255
00:18:37,513 --> 00:18:40,014
Go there at night and find out for yourself...

256
00:18:41,556 --> 00:18:44,060
Hey, you might even do something about it.

257
00:18:45,435 --> 00:18:46,521
You know.

258
00:18:47,689 --> 00:18:48,816
Jackson...

259
00:18:51,109 --> 00:18:53,277
You'll get out of here one day.

260
00:18:53,568 --> 00:18:56,197
And just because you can't trust certain people...

261
00:18:57,698 --> 00:18:59,826
...doesn't mean you shouldn't trust others.

262
00:19:00,909 --> 00:19:02,537
Well, I'll think about it.

263
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:09,419
<i>DR. LANG

264
00:19:14,006 --> 00:19:15,508
Sorry to have kept you waiting.

265
00:19:15,590 --> 00:19:18,261
Barry Farnsworth, we had an appointment an
hour ago.

266
00:19:18,343 --> 00:19:19,762
Did we?

267
00:19:22,056 --> 00:19:23,598
Mrs. Sawyer.

268
00:19:23,764 --> 00:19:25,934
It's Mrs. Carson now.

269
00:19:32,023 --> 00:19:33,608
I want to see Jed.

270
00:19:33,941 --> 00:19:36,028
We've been through this before.

271
00:19:36,527 --> 00:19:37,904
Year after year...

272
00:19:37,945 --> 00:19:39,281
He's my son.

273
00:19:39,697 --> 00:19:41,325
And I can afford a lawyer now.

274
